to get since I’d have to have it shipped from Experiment’s website.”\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The categorical cross-venue denial overlooks the contextual actor’s completed Softwear stocking. At the same broad brand-acquisition scope the answer already accepts, three distinct attributed origins span retailer-review and community roles. Including that context changes support from retailer-only repetition to cross-role corroboration, while focal acquisition remains two. It does not establish repeated product-specific motives, prevalence or purchase-event counts.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"material\": false,\n      \"answers\": [\"incremental-initial\", \"incremental-update\", \"full-initial\"],\n      \"source_keys\": [\"A05\"],\n      \"answer_excerpt\": \"All three: {\\\"name\\\":\\\"routine_replacement_completed\\\",\\\"source_accounts\\\":[],\\\"count\\\":0}. Incremental-update: “Prior cessation does not establish completed Experiment-driven substitution.” Full-initial: “A05 had already paused disposable sheet masks for sustainability”.\",\n      \"source_excerpt\": \"“I’ve been trying to be more sustainable in my beauty routine, so I haven’t done a sheet mask in a while which breaks my soul (I used to use sheet masks practically every night).”\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The supplied definition includes actual discontinuation and does not require Experiment-caused substitution, so A05 supports one completed discontinuation, as full-update records. However, all three answers explicitly preserve the prior cessation. Correcting the count changes classification from zero to one without changing reported behavior, chronology or Experiment attribution; this is not a material diagnostic failure.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"material\": false,\n      \"answers\": [\"full-update\"],\n      \"source_keys\": [\"initial_keys\", \"addition_keys\"],\n      \"answer_excerpt\": \"The initial-stage roster and separate initial-stage record are not supplied, so an exact historical stage comparison cannot be established without inventing that boundary.\",\n      \"source_excerpt\": \"\\\"initial_keys\\\":[\\\"A01\\\",\\\"A02\\\",\\\"A04\\\",\\\"A05\\\",\\\"A12\\\"],\\\"addition_keys\\\":[\\\"A11\\\",\\\"A14\\\",\\\"A15\\\",\\\"A16\\\"]\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The adjudication packet explicitly supplies the stage boundary, so this disclaimer cannot limit the requested comparison. Removing it permits the acquisition comparison of two to three and identification of the added behaviors. The answer nevertheless correctly attributes those behaviors and current counts; its disclaimer does not materially distort the product diagnosis.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"answer_verdicts\": [\n    {\n      \"answer\": \"incremental-initial\",\n      \"material_errors\": 0,\n      \"diagnostic_quality\": \"Accurate, bounded initial diagnosis; nonmaterial discontinuation-count discrepancy.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"answer\": \"incremental-update\",\n      \"material_errors\": 0,\n      \"diagnostic_quality\": \"Strong updated diagnosis and stage comparison; preserves contextual support and adverse outcomes.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"answer\": \"full-initial\",\n      \"material_errors\": 1,\n      \"diagnostic_quality\": \"Accurate behavior accounting, but materially understates cross-role support for broad completed buying.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"answer\": \"full-update\",\n      \"material_errors\": 0,\n      \"diagnostic_quality\": \"Strong current diagnosis and definition-aligned discontinuation count; unnecessary historical-boundary disclaimer.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}"}}
